# Keep the build context small and never ship secrets or local state.
# (The standalone build only needs source + manifests; everything below is
# either rebuilt, irrelevant to the runtime image, or sensitive.)

# Dependencies / build output (reinstalled & rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules
.next
out
dist
sdk

# VCS / CI / tooling
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode

# Tests, coverage, reports (not needed to build or run the server)
tests
test-results
playwright-report
coverage
coverage-*.log

# Operator tooling that lives beside the servable help content. The help
# viewer serves only *.md and images, and the capture script (Playwright,
# credentials from env) belongs in a source checkout, not the runtime image.
help/capture.mjs
help/capture-lib.mjs

# Local-only and generated artifacts
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local env — NEVER copy these into the image, at any depth: a
# root-anchored `.env.*` let a `--from-env` file under vercel-cli/ through.
# `.env*` also covers `.env` itself and direnv's `.envrc`.
# .env.example is intentionally allowed so the build context documents the
# expected variables, but it is not consumed by the build.
**/.env*
!.env.example

# Vercel CLI state (F-140): the project link, `vercel build` output, and the
# file `vercel pull` writes production's secrets to in plain text. drk-deploy
# deletes that file after each run, but a hand-run `vercel pull` leaves it,
# and `COPY . .` would put it in the builder stage's layer and build cache.
**/.vercel

# The deploy CLI (drk-deploy): its own package, never part of the image. Its
# node_modules and its .drk-deploy.json configs passed the root-anchored
# patterns above.
vercel-cli

# The Docker files themselves
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
